<article class="env-lemma" id="09XR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09XR">Lemma <span data-tag="09XR">59.79.2</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of schemes. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be an injective abelian sheaf on $Z_{\acute{e}tale}$. Then $\mathcal{H}^ p_ Z(i_*\mathcal{G}) = 0$ for $p > 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the functor $i_*$ is exact and transforms injective abelian sheaves into injective abelian sheaves (Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0730" data-tag="0730">21.14.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>